      "page_title": "Cost Limits, Trade-offs & Cheat Sheet",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Cost Limits",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Score each field, multiply by list-size arguments",
            "Reject over budget BEFORE anything executes",
            "`maxDepth: 10` stops `friends { friends { ... } }`",
            "Flexibility means the server cannot predict its workload"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Alias-bombing is a DoS",
          "text": "A thousand aliased copies of one expensive field multiply server work while looking like a single small query. Depth limiting misses it — cap aliases per operation, or use cost analysis that counts each aliased copy."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "vs REST"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Concern",
            "REST",
            "GraphQL"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Cache",
              "URL CDN",
              "normalized client"
            ],
            [
              "Batching",
              "composite route",
              "DataLoader"
            ],
            [
              "Errors",
              "status codes",
              "`errors[]` at 200"
            ],
            [
              "Versioning",
              "`/v2/`",
              "`@deprecated`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Over-fetching solved: ask for exactly your fields",
            "Under-fetching solved: nest instead of waterfalling",
            "Offset paging drifts; cursors are the stable default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Connections"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "feed(first: 10, after: $cur) {",
            "  edges { node { id } cursor }",
            "  pageInfo { hasNextPage",
            "             endCursor } }"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "When NOT To Use It"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Simple CRUD with a single consumer",
            "Upload and download heavy APIs",
            "When HTTP caching is the whole strategy",
            "Small app: fetch + REST is genuinely simpler"
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Cheat Sheet"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "query Name($v: Type! = def) { ... }",
            "fragment F on T { fields }   ...F",
            "key: field(args) @include(if: $flag)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Prod hardening",
          "items": [
            "Gate or disable introspection",
            "Accept persisted queries only",
            "Depth + cost limit on every operation",
            "Normalized caches are a real client cost"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Before you ship it",
          "text": "Named, variables typed, fragments colocated, `__typename` on unions, `id` returned on mutation payloads, cost within budget."
        }
      ]
    }
